// ProjectDeliveryS682 — Sprint 682: The gating family joins keel gate and keel audit. Under D0452 (accepted on the human's own words 2026-09-12, brief copy-out) the ten gating verbs that are not already routers - validate, check, check-engine, guard, rules, assured, adoption-check, audit-history, audit-adherence, audit-ci-runs - leave the top-level dispatch and become sub-verbs of `keel gate` (validate, check, check-engine, guard, rules, assured, adoption-check) and `keel audit` (history, adherence, ci-runs), each keeping its word and its arguments, in the sprint 512 shape (D0273): a committed transform rewrites every call site in the same commit as the removal, no alias window, and the pre-fold binary is held byte-equal to the post-fold binary on stdout, stderr and exit code over a green tree, a red tree and a workspace root, because a gate's exit code is its answer. The hooks under .githooks and the workflows under .github/workflows are rewritten in the same commit and exercised by it. Delivers the fourth of the five folds dcRemainingCliFamilies names; the dispatch count hardening reads drops 49 to 39. CHANGE.. EXECUTE. 8 pts.
